																		Opinion and suggestions
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nyctheboss" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6491959); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6491959&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606121087" alt="NyctheBoss" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6491959)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nyctheboss" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6491959); return false;" >NyctheBoss</a></span> <span class="odate time_1591198550 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Jun 2020 15:35</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4675273">
									

<p>So first of all, I really liked this read. Maybe because I'm new, but I think it's pretty original! It's short and simple to understand, and the tone is kept more or less the same throughout the whole piece.</p>
<p>However, as did a lot of people say already, the dialogue is pretty meh. I would like to propose some changes regarding sentence structure, seen that it's already been talked about in this discussion.</p>
<p><em>Test B</em></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Suggestion&nbsp;1</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Fold&nbsp;suggestion&nbsp;1</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>D-90353 was sent into the testing chamber and upon spotting D-90353, SCP-5046-1 headed towards him</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I had to reread the sentence at least two times because of the wierd wording here. Repeating D-90353's name just makes it look like there are two of them, or that there you meant someone else. Instead, maybe try:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Upon spotting D-90353 entering the testing chamber, SCP-5046-1 headed towards him</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That way, the order of events is clearer and the sentence looks more polished :D</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Suggestion&nbsp;2</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Fold&nbsp;suggestion&nbsp;2</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>(&#8230;)D-90353 was instructed to remove SCP-5046 and did so.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This one was easy to understand, but unpleasant to look at. It's ending just seems &quot;anti-climatic&quot;, like you used a lot of long words just to end it with &quot;and did so&quot;. I think it would look better if it was:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>(&#8230;)D-90353 was instructed to remove SCP-5046, which it did.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Note that I used &quot;it&quot;, to reinforce that the foundation tends to dehumanize D-class personnel.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><em>Test E</em></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Suggestion&nbsp;3</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Fold&nbsp;suggestion&nbsp;3</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5046-1: Yes. I was created to be… Well a companion. I'm naturally a pretty friendly person. I exist primarily to be well… a pet I guess.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Here, I see that you used ellipsis to make it look like thinking between sentences. But in the second half, the thinking doesn't look natural. I would suggest that you moved the second &quot;well&quot; to after the elipsis, but because you already used it pretty early in the sentence, I think just removing it entirely would look better. Also the first well starts with caps, (which I think is a gramatical error) and I reckon it would make it even more natural if there was a comma after it:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5046-1: Yes. I was created to be… well, a companion. I'm naturally a pretty friendly person. I exist primarily to be… a pet I guess.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Suggestion&nbsp;4</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Fold&nbsp;suggestion&nbsp;4</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Perrin: I see… Can you tell me who created you and how</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's missing a question mark :p</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Suggestion&nbsp;5</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Fold&nbsp;suggestion&nbsp;5</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5046-1: Well my creator was- No… Sorry you want to talk to me you're going to have to use something other than a corpse.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sentence is too long, and with no commas it looks like SCP-5046-1 was talking really fast or that there was something behind him that was forcing him to keep talking or he would explode if he kept talking why is this sentence still going on and how do I stop.<br />
I believe there are a few missing words to connect the sentence, it doesn't look finished (with all due respect).</p>
<p>My suggestion is the following:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5046-1: Well my creator was- No… Sorry, but if you want to talk to me you're going to have to use something other than a corpse.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There are a lot of ways to improve it, but I reckon this is the one that makes the less amount of tweaking and the most improvements without changing the sentence's meaning.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>That's it! Sorry if it's too long, but I think the small changes can make a world of diference on the piece as a whole. I don't know if you're going to rewrite it or just edit the page, but whatever you do, I know I'm gonna like it ;)</p>
